ationary and  restricted to a certain area he has free  roam turned on and can shove anywhere on  the map at random now this is why he  appears in the city one minute and then  pops up in the forest the next during  the manga a lot of players run out there  because they believe that he couldn't  travel to that part of the map however  he shut up like what we see in the show  and burned a large part of it during his  attack and the King also has his own  strategies and ways of carrying things  out Beyond just showing up at places  there's actually a method to the madness  and sharabi normally Waits until people  are gathered in one area so you can get  the most amount of players in the  shortest amount of time whereas most  people believe there would be safety in  numbers he disproves that by killing  people in quick succession his entire  tactic is to ambush people and by the  time his blimp has drifted in he's  normally fully set up somewhere and  ready to take everyone out now though  he's a villain he actually views himself  as a hero Because he believes he has an  insight to life that many don't possess  sharabi believes that life is painful  and filled with misery and that by  killing people he's actually saving them  from the pain of it this was a mind  state that was something he developed  after his time as a mercenary which is  what we see in a flashback in the manga  shirabi was highly sought after and when  he was on holiday in Tokyo his old  friend Apache reached out to him with a  job sharabi suspicious of it and he  viewed it as being a mission that was  gonna just be a Slaughter he told Apache  not to do it and said that he'd be  killed if he went ahead with the job  Apache thanked him for being such a good  friend and sharabi basically said that  he's not really a friend and though  they're allies today if they got hired  for opposite jobs they might be on  opposite sides he said they were  business rivals but Apache clearly  didn't see it that way even though he  had a really bad feeling about it drabi  still accepted the job with his  quote-unquote friend and as predicted it  was a complete show the battle was a  Slaughter and they'd indeed been sent in  as sacrificial Lambs upon fleeing the  battlefield both were shot but sharabi  suffered but a flesh wound Apache on the  other hand was in critical condition and  though sharabi had said they weren't  friends he still did whatever he could  to pull his friend out they made it  quite far too but Apache said that he  was just slowing his friend down and  that he should leave him shurabi didn't  want to do this and he rested alongside  him with which is when they both agreed  to meet each other as friends of War on  another Battlefield after this Apache  asked him to kill him which sharabi  didn't really want to do however Apache  explained that he was suffering and that  the rest of his life would be a misery  he asked sharabi to kill him and said  that he would save him from the agony  that his life was gonna be this is where  we saw him in the vision and he killed  Apache at this point which is where he  also developed the Mind state that he  should ease people of the burden of  their lives now when the media struck  shrabi was closer to the center of the  blast and thus he ended before the main  players that we end up following in the  show as the show States time moves  differently in Borderland the entire  time arisu spent down there it was just  a minute in our world so if someone was  hit even just 10 seconds earlier then  they'd arrive down there months earlier  kyum and shirabi both arrived five  months before Ari suited and thus they  had time to play out an entire cycle  kyuma actually worked alongside shirabi  and Mira who all became friends she  bumped into him while he was burying a  body and it turned out that sharabi had  actually been going through Borderland  and burying those that had been killed  he didn't want to leave the corpses  behind f